+# Independent management page protocol V1
+
+Extract this directory from the published executable. Compile Java providers against the same
+published executable. The SDK and npm package are the only host inputs for independent extensions.
+`contract.json` pins the supported component package and integrity, language IDs and fallback.
+`index.d.ts` is the ESM protocol; `locales.mjs` resolves public locale aliases.
+
+Provide one `UiExtensionProviderV1` bean with Micronaut annotation processor indexes. Declare
+`UiExtensionDescriptorV1(1,id,"ui-extensions/"+id,entry,styles,files,titles,capabilityPath)`.
+Each file has a lowercase SHA-256 and MIME. Resources must exist under that exact classpath root.
+The classloader is shared: namespace and hash validate content, not classloader source isolation.
+Duplicate IDs, invalid metadata and missing or mismatched files reject registrations. Limits are
+16 MiB per file, 64 MiB per extension, 128 MiB per registry. Restart the JVM after changing jars.
+
+The host route is `/ui/{tenant}/extensions/{id}/...`. The host owns navigation and lifetime;
+the module owns its app and ShadowRoot. Never add extension styles to document. Load only
+context.styles inside the root, inherit host fonts and consume resolved theme data. The initial
+supported components are buttons, inputs and tables. Use routed details, inline confirmation,
+and extension-owned vue-i18n pagination. Dialogs, popovers and complex dropdowns are unsupported.
+
+At build time apply `prepareShadowStyles(css,postcss)` from `shadow-styles.mjs` to CSS generated
+from the pinned public component package. Pass the consumer's PostCSS 8 parser; the helper has
+no dependency on host source or framework instances. It adapts known root selectors and removes
+font declarations. Put application content under `.extension-body`, set theme classes on the
+shadow host and inherit the loaded host font. A future component package requires new compatibility
+validation; this helper is not an adapter for arbitrary third-party stylesheets.
+
+Export `contractVersion=1` and `mount(container,context)` returning update/unmount. Mount and update
+can be asynchronous. Unmount must be idempotent. The host aborts on navigation, serializes updates,
+retains the latest pending context and cleans late mount results. Lifecycle timeout is 5 seconds;
+trusted extension code must stop effects on abort because JavaScript is not a security sandbox.
+
+`navigate` accepts only root-relative extension paths. `request` accepts same-origin
+`/api/v1/{tenant}/...` with query parameters, includes cookies and write CSRF, and returns standard
+Response including 401/403. It rejects redirects, fragments, encoded path ambiguity and external
+origins. The server continues to authorize every API request.
+
+Discovery returns metadata with 200 and hides management entries unless explicit SYSTEM permission
+allows them; no-RBAC deployments use their existing instance authentication boundary. Capability
+is an optional same-origin GET returning `{allowed:true}` and affects menu visibility only.
+It never authorizes API operations. Direct route access still encounters API authorization.
+
+Use locale-wrapped `<locale>.json` files and your own vue-i18n instance with fallback `en`.
+Run `node check-translations.mjs path/to/translations`; failure includes missing, extra, empty
+messages and interpolation differences for all public locales. The checker does not translate
+messages or prove translation quality. No host-internal JSON import is supported.
diff --git a/webserver/src/main/resources/META-INF/kestra/ui-sdk/v1/check-translations.mjs b/webserver/src/main/resources/META-INF/kestra/ui-sdk/v1/check-translations.mjs
